# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. `ettle init <room>` reports which of these
# you have and what each missing one costs you; docs/LINEAR_SETUP.md is how to get
# each. Distilling and reconciling run locally — your raw notes never leave the
# machine, whichever bus you use.

# Required. Distill + reconcile. One per ROOM, not one per person: a teammate
# driving ettle from their own agent distills client-side and needs no key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Linear (the default bus for a team already on Linear + Claude Code) --------

# Required for a linear:// room. A personal member key: Linear → Settings →
# Security & access → Personal API keys. Carries the atom documents and reads
# teammates' agent replies.
# LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_...

# Needed only the FIRST time a room is set up, to create its project (ettle-<room>).
# Ignored once the project exists, so only the first person in a room needs it.
# LINEAR_TEAM_ID=...

# Optional — escalation ONLY: posting a tangle to the room's coordination issue for
# teammates who don't run ettle. An OAuth app-actor token (actor=app); the member
# key can read agent activities but cannot post them. docs/LINEAR_SETUP.md walks it.
# LINEAR_AGENT_TOKEN=lin_oauth_...

# --- GitHub (the same shape for a team on GitHub instead of Linear) -------------

# For a github://<owner>/<repo>[/<room>] room: a token with `repo` scope. Usually
# you need nothing here — ettle falls back to the credential `gh auth login`
# already stored. PRIVATE repos only; the transport refuses a public one, because
# a public repo's Discussions are readable by anyone on the internet.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...

# --- Everything below is the no-Linear fallback --------------------------------

# Distributed NATS bus (only the -tags nats build). Use a tls:// URL and creds
# off localhost — the bus carries your typed atoms.
# NATS_URL=tls://nats.example.com:4222
# NATS_CREDS=/path/to/ettle.creds
# ETTLE_TEAM=your-team

# gemot endpoint for contested tangles (pass via -gemot, or set and read it
# yourself). Use https:// with auth in production — the crux is sensitive.
# ETTLE_GEMOT=https://gemot.example/mcp
